A service with 8 workers and 0.25s of work per request: capacity 32 requests a second.

                            served/s  p50, first half  p50, second half
  closed loop,  8 users         30.0            0.26s             0.26s
  closed loop, 64 users         30.0            2.05s             2.05s
  open loop, 30 req/s           29.1            0.26s             0.26s
  open loop, 36 req/s           30.0            0.57s             1.19s

Sixty-four closed-loop users push the service past capacity, and the test reports a
steady state: 2.05s early, 2.05s late. It cannot report anything else,
because each user waits for an answer before asking again, so the queue never grows
longer than the number of users. Open-loop arrivals just above capacity do what real
users do: the median wait went from 0.57s in the first half to 1.19s in the
second, and it keeps growing for as long as the arrivals continue. A load test that
cannot show that has been coordinated with the thing it was meant to stress.
